From 29ed84c6a103b87048fd66121d4873c2db4259de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WinterYukky <49480575+WinterYukky@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 01:24:13 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] API: add batched getSymbolDocumentations (JSDoc tags +
 documentation comment for many symbols in one request)

Clients that document large libraries (e.g. jsii generating multi-language
bindings for aws-cdk-lib) need the JSDoc tags and the rendered documentation
comment for every exported symbol. Doing that with the per-symbol
getJsDocTags / getDocumentationComment methods costs two round-trips per
symbol, and routing those through the generic batchRequests mechanism was
measured to be slower than the individual calls on 7.1.0-beta because the
per-request payload encoding dominates.

This adds a dedicated checker method, getSymbolDocumentations(symbols), that
returns, per input symbol and in input order, exactly what the two individual
methods would return. The server resolves every symbol against the same
checker setup; a symbol that would fail the individual call fails the batch
the same way. The sync API and proto typings are regenerated, and tests cover
parity with the individual calls plus the sync/generator equivalence.
